    "findings": [
      "Switching to GPT-6 Luna on the same 178 cases cut wrong proposals from 13 to 3, at less than half the list-price cost, but it resolved 50 payments instead of 61. Every payment GPT-6 Luna resolved, DeepSeek also resolved.",
      "Value of wrong proposals counts the full payment of each wrong proposal. GPT-6 Luna's held-out error put the cash on the right invoice and missed only a credit note, MXN 2,262.00.",
      "The biggest gap is still credit notes: the candidate builder never pairs a single invoice with a credit note. Two of GPT-6 Luna's three errors come from it, as did six of DeepSeek's thirteen.",
      "GPT-6 Luna declined notes that describe invoices without numbering them (none of 15 resolved, against DeepSeek's 5). One of its responses failed validation and went to a person.",
      "37 of the answerable cases that went to review had no remittance note, so no model was called."
    ],
